1
00:05:51,428 --> 00:05:57,428
The key to the future is finally unearthed.

2
00:11:42,857 --> 00:11:48,857
Blade Runner 2049 is a science fiction, drama film directed by Denis Villeneuve.

3
00:17:34,285 --> 00:17:40,285
Thirty years after the events of the first film, a new blade runner, LAPD Officer K, unearths a
long-buried secret that has the potential to plunge what's left of society into chaos.

4
00:23:25,714 --> 00:23:31,714
K's discovery leads him on a quest to find Rick Deckard, a former
LAPD blade runner who has been missing for 30 years.

5
00:29:17,142 --> 00:29:23,142
'K', played by Ryan Gosling.

6
00:35:08,571 --> 00:35:14,571
Rick Deckard, played by Harrison Ford.

7
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Joi, played by Ana de Armas.

8
00:46:51,428 --> 00:46:57,428
Sapper Morton, played by Dave Bautista.

9
00:52:42,857 --> 00:52:48,857
Lieutenant Joshi, played by Robin Wright.

10
00:58:34,285 --> 00:58:40,285
Luv, played by Sylvia Hoeks.

11
01:04:25,714 --> 01:04:31,714
Blade Runner 2049 is a 2017 American epic neo-noir science fiction film directed by Denis Villeneuve
from a screenplay by Hampton Fancher and Michael Green, based on a story by Fancher.

12
01:10:17,142 --> 01:10:23,142
A sequel to Blade Runner (1982), the film stars Ryan Gosling and Harrison Ford, with Ana de Armas, Sylvia
Hoeks, Robin Wright, Mackenzie Davis, Dave Bautista, and Jared Leto in supporting roles.

13
01:16:08,571 --> 01:16:14,571
Ford and Edward James Olmos reprise their roles from the
previous film as Rick Deckard and Gaff, respectively.

14
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:06,000
Gosling plays K, a "blade runner" who uncovers a secret that threatens
to destabilize society and the course of civilization.

15
01:27:51,428 --> 01:27:57,428
Ideas for a Blade Runner sequel were first proposed in the 1990s,
but licensing issues stalled their development.

16
01:33:42,857 --> 01:33:48,857
Andrew Kosove and Broderick Johnson obtained the film rights from Bud Yorkin.

17
01:39:34,285 --> 01:39:40,285
Ridley Scott stepped down as the film's initial director and worked as an
executive producer, while Villeneuve was later appointed to direct.

18
01:45:25,714 --> 01:45:31,714
Blade Runner 2049 was financed through a partnership between Alcon Entertainment and
Sony Pictures, as well as a Hungarian government-funded tax rebate.

19
01:51:17,142 --> 01:51:23,142
Warner Bros., which had distributed its predecessor, released the film on behalf of Alcon
in North America, while Sony handled distribution in international markets.

20
01:57:08,571 --> 01:57:14,571
Principal photography took place mostly at two soundstages in
Budapest over four months from July to November 2016.

21
02:03:00,000 --> 02:03:06,000
Blade Runner 2049 premiered at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles, California on
October 3, 2017, and was released in the United States on October 6.

22
02:08:51,428 --> 02:08:57,428
The film received acclaim from critics, who praised multiple aspects including cast
performances, directing, cinematography, and faithfulness to the previous film.

23
02:14:42,857 --> 02:14:48,857
However, it was a box office flop, grossing $276.6 million worldwide against a production budget of
$150–185 million and failing to reach its estimated break-even point of $400 million.

24
02:20:34,285 --> 02:20:40,285
Among its numerous accolades, Blade Runner 2049 received Academy Awards for Best Cinematography and Best Visual Effects out of five
nominations, and eight British Academy Film Awards nominations, winning for Best Cinematography and Best Special Visual Effects.

25
02:26:25,714 --> 02:26:31,714
A sequel television series, Blade Runner 2099, is in development at Amazon
Studios, with Scott set to return as executive producer.

26
02:32:17,142 --> 02:32:23,142
The film explores themes of future, android, bounty hunter,
artificial intelligence (a.i.), genetics.

27
02:38:08,571 --> 02:38:14,571
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and emotional.
